  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/E13682">Remark <span data-tag="E13682">7.2.2.23</span>.</a> Since the class of morphisms $f: X \rightarrow S$ which belong to $\calX ^{\Delta ^1}$ is stable under pullback, we can apply Corollary <a href="/tag/20018F" data-tag="20018F">2.4.7.12</a> (which asserts that $p: \Fun (\Delta ^1,\calX ) \rightarrow \Fun ( \{ 1\} , \calX )$ is a Cartesian fibration), Lemma <a href="/tag/47E2AF" data-tag="47E2AF">6.1.1.1</a> (which characterizes the $p$-Cartesian morphisms of $\Fun (\Delta ^1,\calX )$), and Corollary <a href="/tag/7D67FE" data-tag="7D67FE">2.4.2.5</a> to deduce that the projection $\Gerb _{n}(\calX ) \rightarrow \calX $ is a right fibration. </p>
